<title>SWITZERLAND: Clariant shares suspended from trading.</title>
<headline>Clariant shares suspended from trading.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Swiss chemicals firm Clariant AG were suspended from trading on the Swiss Exchange on Tuesday at the company's request, an exchange spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>She added the shares would be suspended until further notice from the company and it was not clear when this would happen.</p>
<p>Registered shares in Clariant were suspended around 1104 GMT and were last traded at 459 Swiss francs, up 11 francs from Monday's close.</p>
<p>Trading volume in Clariant was relatively heavy with 32,518 shares traded.  </p>
<p>Earlier German chemicals firm Hoechst AG said in Frankfurt that it would take a sizable minority stake in Clariant as part of a merger of their specialty chemical activities.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
